<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8" />
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
<title>RelBench Leaderboard · Stanford Tabular and Relational Project (STAR)</title>
<meta name="description" content="RelBench leaderboard. Test-set results for predictive machine learning on relational databases across regression, classification, and recommendation tasks." />
<meta property="og:title" content="RelBench Leaderboard" />
<meta property="og:description" content="Test-set results on the RelBench tasks." />
<link rel="canonical" href="https://star-project.stanford.edu/relbench/leaderboard/" />
<meta property="og:site_name" content="Stanford Tabular and Relational Project" />
<meta property="og:type" content="website" />
<meta property="og:url" content="https://star-project.stanford.edu/relbench/leaderboard/" />
<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary" />
<meta name="twitter:title" content="RelBench Leaderboard" />
<meta name="twitter:description" content="Test-set results on the RelBench tasks." />
<link rel="icon" href="/assets/img/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Newsreader:ital,opsz,wght@0,6..72,400;0,6..72,500;0,6..72,600;1,6..72,400;1,6..72,500&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/style.css?v=b14b726" />
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/leaderboard.css?v=b14b726" />
</head>
<body class="lb-page">

<!-- NAV -->
<header class="nav">
  <div class="nav-inner">
    <a class="brand" href="/">
      <span class="glyph"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
      <span class="brand-name">Stanford Tabular and Relational (STAR) Project</span>
    </a>
    <button class="nav-toggle" aria-label="Menu"><span></span></button>
    <nav class="nav-links">
      <a href="/publications">Publications</a>
      <a href="/#resources">Resources</a>
      <a href="/#talks">Talks</a>
      <a href="/#people">People</a>
      <a class="nav-btn" href="https://github.com/stanford-star" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a>
      <a class="nav-btn" href="https://huggingface.co/stanford-star" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Hugging Face ↗</a>
    </nav>
  </div>
</header>

<!-- HERO -->
<section class="hero paper-hero">
  <canvas class="hero-canvas" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
  <div class="hero-fade"></div>
  <div class="paper-hero-inner">
    <a class="back-link" href="/relbench"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M19 12H5M11 18l-6-6 6-6"/></svg> RelBench</a>
    <p class="paper-venue reveal"><span class="venue-badge">Leaderboard</span> 31 tasks · self-reported test results</p>
    <h1 class="reveal d1">RelBench Leaderboard</h1>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- LEADERBOARD -->
<section class="lb-section" style="padding: 0 0 72px">
  <div class="wrap">
    <section id="lb">
      <div class="tabbar">
        <div id="splits" class="tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Leaderboard"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="lb-above">
        <p id="metric" class="lb-metric"></p>
        <button id="task-hint" class="lb-hint" type="button" aria-controls="lb-panel">task-wise results <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></button>
      </div>
      <div class="table-wrap" id="lb-panel" role="tabpanel">
        <table id="board"><caption class="sr-only"></caption><thead></thead><tbody></tbody></table>
      </div>
      <p id="empty" class="empty" hidden>No entries yet.</p>
      <p class="lb-foot"><span id="count"></span></p>

      <div class="lb-note">
        <p>The RelBench leaderboard (<a href="/relbench/leaderboard/submit/">submit ↗</a>) uses self-reported prediction files. We place no restriction on submissions (e.g. runtime, hyperparameter-tuning, etc.) except the following:</p>
        <ol>
          <li>For all submissions, any info at or in the future of the prediction time is off-limits.</li>
          <li>For in-context submissions, gradient-based training on the target DB is not allowed.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>For a more controlled and transparent evaluation on RelBench tasks, please see <a href="https://github.com/PriorLabs/relarena" target="_blank" rel="noopener">RelArena ↗</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- FOOTER -->
<footer class="footer">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="footer-top">
      <div>
        <div class="f-brand">Stanford Tabular and Relational (STAR) Project</div>
        <p class="f-desc">Foundation models, datasets, and benchmarks for tabular and relational data. Open science from Stanford University.</p>
      </div>
      <div><h4>Artifacts</h4><ul><li><a href="https://huggingface.co/datasets/stanford-star/relbench-v1" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Hugging Face</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/stanford-star/relbench" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a></li><li><a href="/relbench">RelBench overview</a></li></ul></div>
      <div><h4>Lab</h4><ul><li><a href="https://snap.stanford.edu" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SNAP Group</a></li><li><a href="https://www.stanford.edu" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Stanford University</a></li></ul></div>
    </div>
    <div class="footer-bottom">
      <span>© <span data-year>2026</span> Stanford Tabular and Relational Project</span>
      <span>star-project.stanford.edu/relbench/leaderboard</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</footer>

